        "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Cost</strong> nothing · <strong>Requirements</strong> You are in <strong>Severance</strong></p><hr /><p><em>Howl.</em> Every wolf you have left converges on one point and goes off together.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> At least one wolf remains.</p><p><strong>40-foot burst</strong> within 120 feet, basic Reflex, <strong>force</strong> damage.</p><p>You expend <strong>all</strong> remaining wolves and regain none for the rest of the encounter. If you had <strong>five or more</strong>, creatures that critically fail are also knocked <strong>prone</strong> and <strong>stunned 1</strong>.</p><hr /><p><strong>&#9888; Extrapolated</strong> &mdash; the soul-splitting wolves are canon.</p><hr /><p><strong>Waning.</strong> The damage is <strong>20d6</strong> if used in the first round of Severance, and two dice fewer each round after &mdash; 18d6, 16d6, 14d6, 12d6, 10d6, and <strong>8d6</strong> in the seventh. After the seventh round this cannot be used at all.</p><p><strong>Using this ends Severance</strong>, whether you want it to or not.</p>"
